You use the number pad, not the arrow keys. With the numberpad option 
on, it interprets '2' (for example) as 'down', easily verified by using 
the top row numbers. It can be hard to get your telnet client to send 
arrows, because it may think you're trying to cycle through commands or 
edit a line. Besides, the number pad has the '5' key for quick moving, 
something I would die without.

